  "_notes": {
    "scale": "Barry 240 px standing / Peaux 215 px (D-013), 60 PPU. Pair frames S1-S3/R1-R3 share one factor (0.30) so contact points line up; singles scaled to match the stand sprites (S4/S5 0.245, R4/R5 0.245, R6 0.255, R7 0.225).",
    "pair_spacing": "S1-S3/R1-R3 drawn with the feet/roots 132 px apart; every pair pivot moved 30 px toward the opponent (D-032/D-033) so the pair lines up at lockUpPairSpacing 1.2 (72 px).",
    "flip": "Barry frames stored facing left; S1-S2 unflipped while Barry faces left (lock-up), S3-S5 drawn flipped (he faces the throw direction). R1-R3 follow Locked Up: stored facing left, flipped while Peaux faces right. R4-R7 stored for a throw to screen-right (slammer on the left): unflipped while the throw goes right, flipped when it goes left. R6 lies head-left.",
    "receiver_roots": "R4-R7 pivot = bottom centre of the cell = body centre on the ground; root = slammer feet centre + root_offset_from_slammer_feet_px along the throw (R6 382 = 1.59 x 240 median; vary +-10%). lowest_pixel_above_ground is baked in as empty rows (R7 bounce 17 px).",
    "stand_return": "S5 -> stand_front: S5 feet centre is 30 px from the root (pivot shift), stand_front feet are at the root, so the feet jump 30 px on the return to stand_front unless presentation compensates.",
    "R6": "Shared downed sprite for every knockdown (designer decision): bottom row of the cell = ground line.",
    "v5b": "S1b/S2b/R1b/R2b (files *5b_*) replace the designer-rejected S1/S2/R1/R2 (2026-11-16). Same conventions as S1/S2/R1/R2: 132 px spacing, pivot shifted 30 px toward the opponent, Barry stored facing left and unflipped during the lift, R stored facing left and flipped while Peaux faces right. Pair factor 0.28 on the 1008 px flux-2-pro outputs (matched by eye to the approved S3 head/cap/boot size).",
    "v5c": "S1c/S2c/R1c/R2c (files *5c_*) = S1b/S2b/R1b/R2b with only Barry's near (left) hand moved flat onto Peaux's chest/torso (designer request 2026-11-16). Same conventions and same pair factor 0.28 as v5b; feet, ground and roots unchanged, so contact with S3/R3 lines up as before. Cell widths/pivots of S2c and R1c differ from v5b only because the cell is cut symmetric around the feet and the visible bbox changed; roots are the same."
  },
